---
Title: Southern Banana Pudding
Servings: 10
Tags: Sweet Shack, Southern
Link: https://grilledcheesesocial.com/2024/09/16/southern-banana-pudding-condesned-milk/#recipe
---

In a #large bowl{}, add @Instant Cheesecake Pudding Mix{5 oz} to cold @Milk{2 cups}. Use a hand mixer and beat on high for ~{2 minutes}.

Set aside to thicken.

In another #large bowl{}, beat together:
- @Cream Cheese{8 oz}
- @Sweetened Condensed Milk{14 oz}
- @Vanilla{2 teaspoons}
Set aside

Fold the mixtures together until smooth and creamy.

Carefully fold in the @Cool Whip{1 tub} until well combined.

Layer the dish starting from the bottom with:
- @Vanilla Wafers{1/2 package}
- @Bananas{4}
- Pudding Mixture
- crumbed @Vanilla Wafers{1/2 package}

Chill for ~{2 hours}.


Notes: 
1. You want bananas that are all yellow with minimal brown spots. If they are too ripe, they will be mushy and not hold up well in the pudding.
2. You can whip Heavy Whipping Cream{1 cup} instead of using Cool Whip if you prefer a more natural option. Just make sure to whip it until stiff peaks form before folding it into the pudding mixture.
3. I prefer Cheesecake pudding but traditional Vanilla pudding or Banana pudding will work as well. You can also use a combination for a unique flavor.